{"parentUuid":"044377e9-68c9-446c-82b0-2bb97548c1bb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Artifact","toolUseID":"toolu_01LqawJbqibZ2QdtYDAha76i","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"da5f8841-096a-4b09-8f58-04074bff697a\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"agent-plugins\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Artifact\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":71},"type":"attachment","uuid":"68327153-2f7a-4278-981d-76c8b3bbe71b","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:36:26.899Z","session_id":"4835aa55-f51a-493e-9e0f-cf80e9966a0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","sessionId":"da5f8841-096a-4b09-8f58-04074bff697a","version":"2.1.241","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cozy-napping-kay"}
{"parentUuid":"68327153-2f7a-4278-981d-76c8b3bbe71b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14946447 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ba9caf60-fc39-4246-896c-e962322449f1","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:36:26.914Z","session_id":"4835aa55-f51a-493e-9e0f-cf80e9966a0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/agent-plugins","sessionId":"da5f8841-096a-4b09-8f58-04074bff697a","version":"2.1.241","gitBranch":"main","slug":"cozy-napping-kay"}
{"parentUuid":"ba9caf60-fc39-4246-896c-e962322449f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeM2oSV4FQ1w9WHQ4h9j7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Nav question first:** no hamburger — keep the pill row. It's in-page section jumping (8 links), not site navigation, so a hamburger would hide the table-of-contents that's the point of showing it. Fixed a real problem with it instead, below.\n\n**What I found and fixed**, all measured across a 390–1440px width sweep, not just eyeballed:\n\n1. **Nav pills silently overflowed at every width from 390px up to 980px** (scrollable content ~1140px vs. visible 350–808px) with zero visual cue. Added an edge-fade gradient that's live/interactive — it shows on the right when there's more to scroll, disappears at each end, driven by an actual scroll listener (verified via scripted scroll-to-end).\n2. **Diagrams looked lost on tablet/desktop** — capped at their native ~400–440px pixel size, leaving 38–50% dead space inside the diagram card at 700px+ widths. They now scale responsively up to 640px, so they fill the card properly on bigger screens while staying exactly as safe/uncropped on mobile as before (verified: dead space dropped to 13–20% everywhere, no overflow at any tested width).\n3. Added subtle zebra striping to table rows for easier scanning on the longer tables (pricing, mechanism, constellation).\n\nReverified with fresh renders at mobile, tablet (768px), and desktop — no regressions, diagrams and tables both look meaningfully more polished at the sizes that were previously weak. Republished to the same URL."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_read_input_tokens":158336,"output_tokens":501,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral